    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-lī^bro</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, āre, v. a.
			3. liber, <i>to take off the rind</i> or
				<i>bark, to peel</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arborem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 11, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radicem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5,
					6, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corticem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					4, 24, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 11, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ramum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 17, 7</span></i>
			. In <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3, 1088</span></i>, the true reading is
			delibare (q. v.).</div>
